// REQUIRES: host-linux-amd64, lldb
// RUN: %gopp build %S/Inputs/generic.gopp -o %t
// RUN: timeout 60 lldb --no-lldbinit -b -s %S/Inputs/generic.lldb %t 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
// P04.08 (decision M8): the same names as gdb-generic.test, in lldb: an
// instance of a generic type is `Name[args]`, the arguments spelled as the
// debugger spells any type (`main.Pair[int64, string]` for a Pair[int,
// string]), a defined type argument with its package, an instance inside an
// instance. The other side: a type that is not generic keeps its name
// (`main.Point`).
// CHECK: @@VARS
// CHECK: (main.Pair[int64, string]) p = {
// CHECK: Key = 1
// CHECK: (main.Box[main.Point]) b = {
// CHECK: V = (X = 3, Y = 4)
// CHECK: (main.Pair[main.Box[int64], float64]) q = {
// CHECK: Key = (V = 5)
// CHECK: @@TYPES
// CHECK: name = "main.Point", byte-size = 16
// CHECK-NOT: main.Point[
